  "notes": "A literary or formal word for an afternoon nap. Composed of {午|ご} (noon) and {睡|すい} (sleep). Commonly used in childcare settings for scheduled nap time. In everyday speech, ⟦{昼寝|ひるね}→昼寝：00106_hirune⟧ is more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {午睡|ごすい}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧とる: to take an afternoon nap\n- {午睡|ごすい}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{時間|じかん}→時間：00468_jikan⟧: nap time\n- {午睡|ごすい}⟦から→から：00504_kara⟧⟦{覚|さ}める→覚める：02058_sameru⟧: to wake from an afternoon nap\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{昼寝|ひるね}→昼寝：00106_hirune⟧: daytime nap — the everyday equivalent, much more common in casual speech\n- ⟦{仮眠|かみん}→仮眠：08333_kamin⟧: short nap, catnap — emphasizes brevity, used at any time of day\n- ⟦{居眠|いねむ}り→居眠り：01822_inemuri⟧: dozing off — unintentional napping, especially while sitting",
